{"duration_api_ms":113875,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a7b58597-b37b-4f17-bdab-57579c23cd1a","total_cost_usd":0.175684,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15940,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":11192,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6478},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15940,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11192,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15940,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15940},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11192,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15940,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.175684,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":6478,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is essentially one ridge at D≈3.385, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 (the upper bound), with only flight_path_angle varying. Along it, flux rises from 227k W/m² at gamma -1.5 to 274.6k at -3.57, and bondline T falls from 417.9 K to 391.1 K. The ridge is capped at the steep end by max_g (margin 4.7e-5 at -3.57) and by heatshield mass fraction (margin 1.4e-4 at D=3.385). Every off-ridge design I can see (the nearly_feasible list) has flux of 440k or more and is dominated. Most of the 8 recent failures are extrapolation refusals at bluntness>1.2 or cone<70, or invalid geometry at lower cone with high bluntness. Hypervolume gains since round 3 have been about 1e-3 or less per round.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-948029610632 (gamma -1.5) and C-81e40e27ff03 (gamma -3.57) bound the ridge, with T from 417.87 to 391.09 K and flux from 227220 to 274570.\",\"C-81e40e27ff03 has max_g 11.999 (margin 4.7e-5), so gamma steeper than about -3.5703 breaks g<=12.\",\"C-0265d5374015 (D=3.3851) has mass-fraction margin 8.6e-5 against 1.45e-4 at D=3.385, so D is capped near 3.3853.\",\"C-3136d3bd2588, C-05edbf22eaa2, C-3d41ce848a30 and C-7db223121090 fail on cd_fore extrapolation at bluntness>1.2 or cone<70, so the corner sits on the surrogate's convex-hull edge.\",\"C-e0197c1bd7dc and C-5608a135cebc are invalid geometries at cone 68 and cone 60 with bluntness 1.2, so high bluntness needs a high cone angle.\",\"Off-ridge points such as C-ab9827dc6929, C-f97dae207371 and C-63aaa0985529 have flux of 438k-515k, so those regions are far from competitive.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak g is set almost entirely by gamma, and mass fraction by roughly D² with a weak dependence on cone and bluntness. Together they pin the low-T end at gamma≈-3.57 and D≈3.385. A large blunt 70° cone gives the highest drag coefficient, hence the lowest ballistic coefficient, so peak heating occurs high in the atmosphere. Shallower gamma lowers flux but lengthens the heat pulse, which raises T, so this trade-off is a smooth monotone curve. Remaining hypervolume gain comes from filling gaps along the curve and from small sensitivity probes at the hull edge (bluntness slightly below 1.2, D slightly changed). Most of this reasoning is inferred from the ridge data and the earlier rounds' notes; the effect of bluntness on flux and T at cone 70 is not directly observed in the rows shown.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The ridge interpolations are reliable to about ±0.3 K and ±500 W/m². The bluntness, cone and D probes are extrapolations from physical reasoning, and the cone 69.8 probe may hit an extrapolation refusal or invalid geometry. Some of my gamma values may duplicate evaluations that are not in the visible tables. Expected hypervolume gain is small, since the ridge is already dense.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-948029610632\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the shallow end of the ridge just off the gamma bound.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5237},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227680,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.48,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the low-flux end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a29bfeb09454\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.6 and -1.68.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":230190,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.42,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-c2d1addc0c7e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.75 and -1.9.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.85},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":234400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":412.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ca9c4b0f355e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.9 and -2.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237610,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-447d95a1c78f\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.15 and -2.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242075,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e1938b62dffb\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.4 and -2.6.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249010,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.07,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-249a4f21af03\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.6 and -2.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.68},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253250,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.78,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-3f1d8b1bcb6a\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.9 and -3.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260875,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.03,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8e0603838c8c\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.2 and -3.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.28},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":267610,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.99,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.4 and -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.27,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.5 and -3.564.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.53},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273620,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.47,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill near the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2db76eed0f16\",\"rationale\":\"Fill in between gamma -3.5 and -3.564, close to the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274340,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.18,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Front gap fill near the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-81e40e27ff03\",\"rationale\":\"Push gamma to the g=12 limit. The estimated g is about 11.9998 from the local slope of about 1.67 g/deg.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5702},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274580,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.085,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extract the last bit of T at the end of the front; it costs at most one slot if g overshoots.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Test a tiny D increase to use the remaining mass-fraction margin of about 1e-4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3852},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272850,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.72,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Check the D sensitivity right at the mass-fraction cap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the inside of the hull edge: bluntness 1.19 at cone 70. It may lower mass fraction, and if drag is barely changed it costs little in flux and T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.19},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Measure the local sensitivity to bluntness at the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Probe a more moderate bluntness of 1.15 at cone 70, which is inside the hull.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Map the bluntness trend to check the corner is optimal.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.1 at cone 70 tests whether the flux trend with nose radius is as expected.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":281000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Further bluntness probe; it may reveal a different flux-T trade-off.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Lower bluntness (1.0) with a smaller D of 3.3, so the heavier shield still meets the mass-fraction limit; this checks for a different trade-off region.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"diameter_m\":3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Exploration off the ridge in the bluntness-D plane.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"Cone 69.8 is slightly inside the upper bound. It may reduce or increase lateral area and mass, but could hit the hull or invalid-geometry limits.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.9,\"feasible\":false},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Check how close the hull edge in cone is and how much T changes near it.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-733cdcb996ae\",\"rationale\":\"D=3.3 gives a sensitivity point for the ballistic coefficient effect on T and flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Quantify the D sensitivity to confirm D is best at its cap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":75506,"type":"result","duration_ms":113965,"uuid":"21bc7623-9b31-4b82-a126-05ebbf7f9373","ttft_stream_ms":2514,"time_to_request_ms":104,"first_content_frame_ms":2515,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
